// LLD of the scene namespace (ds::scene): the whole model laid out once, nested, for a
// viewer that zooms from the system down to a member (SREQ-00013-1, DS-69). Every box is
// measured from what it holds and placed inside its parent in shelves; the layout runs
// twice, with every member and with public members only, and nothing moves between zooms.

package driftspec@ds {

  module scene {

    requirement REQ-00069-1 {
      status: approved
      @refines SREQ-00013-1
      title: The scene shall place every package, module, interface, class, function, enum and member inside its parent, once, apart from its siblings, with and without private members
      text:
        A unit (class, function, enum) is as wide as its longest row and as
        tall as its rows; a module and a package lay their children out in
        shelves no wider than the square root of their area allows; an
        interface sits on its package's border, half outside, as a port. Rows
        read unqualified: run(name) -> vector<Entity>. The second variant
        leaves private members out and shrinks their class; a private class
        keeps its place. Extern modules and expected nodes are not drawn.
      rationale:
        A viewer that shows what fits at each zoom needs places that do not
        move; computed once by ds, the same scene feeds the interactive
        viewer and any snapshot.
      tags: render, scene
    }

    verification VER-00076-1 {
      status: approved
      @requirement REQ-00069-1
      title: Integration tests confirm every class, function and member of ds's design has a place, nested and apart, in both variants
      method: test
      tests:
        tests/integration/ds/scene/test_scene_design.cpp::TestSceneOfTheDesign.EveryClassFunctionAndMemberOfTheModelHasAPlace
        tests/integration/ds/scene/test_scene_design.cpp::TestSceneOfTheDesign.EveryBoxNestsInItsParentApartFromItsSiblings
        tests/integration/ds/scene/test_scene_design.cpp::TestSceneOfTheDesign.WithPrivateMembersHiddenEveryBoxStillNestsAndKeepsApart
    }

    requirement REQ-00070-1 {
      status: approved
      @refines SREQ-00013-1
      title: The viewer shall be one self-contained page that ds writes with the scene inside, titled after the workspace
      text:
        viewer/scene.html is compiled into ds; ds fills it with the scene and
        the workspace's name, so the page opens in a browser as it is, with
        no server and nothing to fetch. What the scene holds never closes the
        page's script. In the page a reader zooms from the system down to a
        member (what fits is shown), sees each kind in its colour and a dot
        for whether a box is linked to a requirement, hides private members,
        and taps a box for its card.
      rationale:
        Owner, 2026-11-06: a JSON is not something to read; the page is what
        a person opens, on a desktop or a phone.
      tags: render, scene, viewer
    }

    verification VER-00077-1 {
      status: approved
      @requirement REQ-00070-1
      title: Integration tests confirm the page of ds's design carries every node of its scene and one script only
      method: test
      tests:
        tests/integration/ds/scene/test_scene_design.cpp::TestSceneOfTheDesign.ThePageOfTheDesignCarriesEveryNodeAndNothingClosesItsScript
    }

    requirement REQ-00071-1 {
      status: approved
      @refines SREQ-00013-1
      title: The viewer shall embed into any HTML document as one iframe, and take a reader's stylesheet over its own
      text:
        ds view --embed prints an iframe whose srcdoc is the whole page, so
        pasting it into a document is all it takes; --height sets its height.
        ds view --css file puts the file after the viewer's own styles: it
        redefines the variables the viewer draws with (background, panels,
        accent, the colour of each kind, the requirement dot, the fonts), and
        cannot close the page's style.
      rationale:
        Owner, 2026-11-06: embed the design in any HTML page with a compact
        command line, and give it the host's look. Colours with a meaning in
        the model belong to the language instead (DS-76).
      tags: render, scene, viewer
    }

    verification VER-00078-1 {
      status: approved
      @requirement REQ-00071-1
      title: Integration tests confirm ds's design embeds as one frame carrying the whole page, and a reader's stylesheet lands after the viewer's
      method: test
      tests:
        tests/integration/ds/scene/test_scene_design.cpp::TestSceneOfTheDesign.TheDesignEmbedsAsOneFrameCarryingTheWholePage
        tests/integration/ds/scene/test_scene_design.cpp::TestSceneOfTheDesign.AReadersStylesheetLandsAfterTheViewersAndCannotCloseIt
    }

    requirement REQ-00072-1 {
      status: approved
      @refines SREQ-00013-1
      title: The scene shall carry each relation between its nodes with its kind and what produces it, the diagrams that show each node, and the title of every requirement linked
      text:
        A link joins the nodes that stand for a relation's ends: a call goes
        from the member whose behaviour writes it to the member it calls,
        with how many times and the sequences that write it; ownership,
        sharing and reference go from the attribute to the type, with their
        multiplicity; inheritance, realisation and use join the boxes they
        name. A relation inside one box is no link. Every diagram of the
        workspace lists the nodes it shows, through the same projection a
        drawing uses. The viewer draws each kind in its notation (a hollow
        triangle for inheritance, a filled diamond for composition, a dashed
        arrow for use, the accent for calls), lifted to the boxes that can be
        seen, and on demand.
      rationale:
        Owner, 2026-11-06: the relations, each in its own rendering, and on
        a box or a relation the detail of where it comes from and where it is
        drawn.
      tags: render, scene, relations
    }

    verification VER-00080-1 {
      status: approved
      @requirement REQ-00072-1
      title: Integration tests confirm every link of ds's design joins two nodes in a kind the viewer draws, every diagram lists nodes of the scene, every requirement has its title
      method: test
      tests:
        tests/integration/ds/scene/test_scene_design.cpp::TestSceneOfTheDesign.EveryLinkJoinsTwoNodesOfTheSceneInOneOfTheKindsItDraws
        tests/integration/ds/scene/test_scene_design.cpp::TestSceneOfTheDesign.EveryDiagramListsTheNodesItShowsAndEveryRequirementHasItsTitle
    }

    verification VER-00081-1 {
      status: approved
      @requirement REQ-00069-1
      title: Integration tests confirm hiding private members makes no box of ds's design wider
      method: test
      tests:
        tests/integration/ds/scene/test_scene_design.cpp::TestSceneOfTheDesign.HidingPrivateMembersMakesNoBoxWider
    }

    requirement REQ-00073-1 {
      status: approved
      @refines SREQ-00013-1
      title: The scene shall carry a tour of every interface operation and public behaviour, each call expanded into the sequence of what it calls, along each named scenario
      text:
        A tour walks a sequence along a scenario (the default path, each
        branch it names, each scenario written apart) with the model's own
        path rule, and expands every call into the sequence it expands to, to
        a depth of seven: a step from the caller to the callee, then the
        steps of the callee, then its answer coming back. Each step knows its
        depth. Private behaviours are replayed inside the public ones that
        reach them. The viewer replays a tour over the structure: the camera
        frames each call, the member called lights up in its box, a sequence
        window keeps the same step, and a depth slider hides what lies below.
      rationale:
        Owner, 2026-11-05 (DS-67, the fourth dimension): the dynamic part
        played over the static one.
      tags: render, scene, behaviour
    }

    verification VER-00082-1 {
      status: approved
      @requirement REQ-00073-1
      title: Integration tests confirm ds check is a tour from the CLI down to the Checker and back, with its syntax-error scenario a tour of its own
      method: test
      tests:
        tests/integration/ds/scene/test_scene_design.cpp::TestSceneOfTheDesign.EveryInterfaceCommandIsATourThatReachesTheModelAndComesBack
    }

    dataclass Step {                         // one step of a tour: a call, or its answer coming back
      @requirement REQ-00073-1
      + from: std::string
      + to: std::string
      + label: std::string
      + depth: int
      + back: bool
    }

    requirement REQ-00074-1 {
      status: approved
      @refines SREQ-00013-1
      title: The scene shall write each behaviour once and name its nodes by index, so the page of a design stays small
      text:
        A behaviour (a sequence along one scenario) is written once with its
        calls in order, each call naming the behaviour it goes on into; a tour
        names the behaviour it starts from, and a viewer expands it to the
        depth asked. Every record of the document is an array whose columns
        the document names in fields, nodes, links, calls and diagrams name
        nodes and behaviours by index, and places are whole units. The page
        of ds's own design stays under 250 KB with the viewer in it.
      rationale:
        Owner, 2026-11-06: keep the page small and usable. The tours of ds
        replayed 3,147 steps out of 229 distinct calls, every identity spelt
        in full: written once, the page went from 593 KB to 146 KB, and depth
        is no longer capped by what was written.
      tags: render, scene, size
    }

    verification VER-00083-1 {
      status: approved
      @requirement REQ-00074-1
      title: Integration tests confirm ds's design writes each behaviour once, its tours replay far more steps than it writes, and its page stays under 250 KB
      method: test
      tests:
        tests/integration/ds/scene/test_scene_design.cpp::TestSceneOfTheDesign.ThePageStaysSmallBecauseEachBehaviourIsWrittenOnce
    }

    dataclass Call {                         // one call of a behaviour: whom it calls, the behaviour it goes on into
      @requirement REQ-00074-1
      + to: std::string
      + label: std::string
      + expands: int
      + result: std::string
    }

    dataclass Behaviour {                    // a sequence along one scenario, its calls in order, written once
      @requirement REQ-00074-1
      + id: std::string
      + subject: std::string
      + scenario: std::string
      + calls: std::vector<Call>
    }

    dataclass Tour {                         // a behaviour a viewer offers to replay
      @requirement REQ-00073-1
      + behaviour: int
      + group: std::string
    }

    dataclass Link {                         // a relation between two nodes, with what produces it
      @requirement REQ-00072-1
      + from: std::string
      + to: std::string
      + kind: std::string
      + count: int
      + multiplicity: std::string
      + sequences: std::vector<std::string>
    }

    dataclass DiagramView {                  // a diagram of the workspace and the nodes it shows
      @requirement REQ-00072-1
      + name: std::string
      + kind: std::string
      + nodes: std::vector<std::string>
    }

    dataclass Box {                          // a rectangle of the scene: one unit is a pixel at zoom 1
      @requirement REQ-00069-1
      + x: double
      + y: double
      + w: double
      + h: double
    }

    dataclass Node {                         // one thing drawn: a package, module, interface, unit or row
      @requirement REQ-00069-1
      + id: std::string
      + kind: std::string
      + parent: std::string
      + label: std::string
      + stereotype: std::string
      + visibility: std::string
      + requirements: std::vector<std::string>
      + owns full: Box
      + lean: bool
      + owns leanBox: Box
    }

    dataclass SceneDocument {                // the scene: its nodes in drawing order and the world each variant spans
      @requirement REQ-00069-1
      + nodes: std::vector<Node>
      + owns world: Box
      + owns leanWorld: Box
      + owns links: std::vector<Link>
      + owns diagrams: std::vector<DiagramView>
      + titles: std::map<std::string, std::string>
      + owns behaviours: std::vector<Behaviour>
      + owns tours: std::vector<Tour>
    }

    class Scene {
      @requirement REQ-00069-1
      - refs model_: model::Model
      + Scene(model: model::Model)
      + build() -> SceneDocument
      + render(pretty: bool) -> std::string
      + page(title: std::string, css: std::string, focus: std::vector<std::string>) -> std::string {
        @requirement REQ-00070-1
        @requirement REQ-00071-1
      }
      - relate(out_document: SceneDocument) -> void {
        @requirement REQ-00072-1
      }
      - tour(out_document: SceneDocument) -> void {
        @requirement REQ-00073-1
      }
      + static frame(page: std::string, title: std::string, height: int) -> std::string {
        @requirement REQ-00071-1
      }
      + static expand(document: SceneDocument, behaviour: int, depth: int) -> std::vector<Step> {
        @requirement REQ-00073-1
      }
    }

    // The layout runs twice, once per variant; build keeps the full one's order and adds
    // the lean place of every node that has one.
    sequence Scene::build {
      loop each variant {
      }
      -> relate(out_document)
      -> tour(out_document)
      return document
    }

    sequence Scene::render {
      -> build() -> document
      return json
    }

    // An iframe whose srcdoc is the whole page, escaped for an attribute: nothing to fetch, and
    // neither the host's styles nor the viewer's leak into the other.
    sequence Scene::frame {
      return frame
    }

    // The viewer template is compiled into ds; the scene, the title and the reader's
    // stylesheet go where it marks them.
    sequence Scene::page {
      -> render(pretty) -> json
      return page
    }
  }
}

diagram CL_SceneNamespace {
  kind: class
  include: driftspec@ds@scene::*
}
